#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Install the 2026-10-20 early-entry scalp fix and three related fixes into ~/kadima-py.

 1. Scalp v2 (kadima/scalp_v2.py): 15-second breakout trigger from index ticks, stop at
    level -/+ 1.5 x 1-min ATR, day-trend gate for scalps, score that penalises chasing,
    priority option-chain poll after a trigger. Installs in SHADOW: v1 keeps trading,
    v2 is logged and written to the Trade Audit as "Scalping v2" for comparison.
 2. Gamma/Celestial auto-trade threshold 60 allowed (trader decision of 10-Oct).
 3. Index lane: index entries use the session issuer's "index" lane, so a stock-scalp
    problem no longer blocks index trading (needs --session-runner, below).
 4. Trade Audit CSV gets "Stage" and "Blocked by" columns.

Anchor-based and fail-closed: every anchor must match the expected number of times or
NOTHING is written. Backups go to <file>.bak-scalpv2-20261020; every Python file is
py_compiled first; a second run changes nothing; --rollback restores everything.
Requires the 19-Oct trend rules (install_trend_rules_20261019.py) to be installed.

Usage (on EC2, after market hours):
  ~/kadima-py/bin/python install_scalp_v2_20261020.py ~/kadima-py               # shadow
  sudo ~/kadima-py/bin/python install_scalp_v2_20261020.py ~/kadima-py \\
       --session-runner /opt/kadima-session-auto/runner.py \\
       --dashboard /var/www/html/dashboard.html                                  # + root-owned files
  ~/kadima-py/bin/python install_scalp_v2_20261020.py ~/kadima-py --live        # v2 trades, priority poll on
  ~/kadima-py/bin/python install_scalp_v2_20261020.py ~/kadima-py --shadow      # back to shadow
  ~/kadima-py/bin/python install_scalp_v2_20261020.py ~/kadima-py --rollback [--session-runner ..] [--dashboard ..]
Then: sudo systemctl restart kadima (and the session timer picks up runner.py on its next run).
Switches live in $KADIMA_DATA_DIR/scalp_v2.json and are re-read every 30 s.
"""
import json, os, py_compile, shutil, sys, tempfile
from pathlib import Path

